WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.470
On 28 September 2022, Hurricane
Ian came ashore on Cayo Costa,

2
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.790
in Lee County, Florida.

3
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.010
This coast is a chain of barrier islands,

4
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:13.570
with about 76 kilometres of beaches.

5
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.850
Ian's winds reached 130 knots.

6
00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:22.490
The sea rose about 3 to 4.6 metres
above the ground at Fort Myers Beach.

7
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.610
In a day, beaches were stripped away.

8
00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.870
So why do people keep
paying to put the sand back?

9
00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.410
In this mission, you'll find
out what erodes this coast,

10
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:35.030
in normal years and in a storm.

11
00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.470
Then you'll weigh up the
ways this coast is managed,

12
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.090
and judge which will last.

13
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.560
Your mission: explain why people keep paying
to put sand back on Florida's beaches.
